/build/
# Downloaded model artifacts — reproducible from config/models.conf, so they
# are never committed. Locally compiled ones (the `source = local` entries)
# have to be dropped back in by hand after a fresh clone.
/models/
*.o
*.user
compile_commands.json
hailort*.log
# Vendor benchmark tools write their reports to the *current directory*, so a
# cross-check run from the repo root litters it. Run them from a scratch dir;
# these patterns are a backstop.
DXBENCHMARK_*.csv
DXBENCHMARK_*.html
DXBENCHMARK_*.json
profiler.json

# CSV logs written by the app (always on; <exe>/../logs/).
logs/
# log files and html reports
*.log
*.html
*.csv
*.png

# ...but NOTHING UNDER docs/ IS INCIDENTAL. That tree is curated by hand: the
# session CSVs kept as evidence, the generated report data, and the report
# pages themselves. The four blanket patterns above would swallow all three
# kinds, and the failure is silent in the way that matters: `git add` on an
# ignored path stages NOTHING, printing a hint and exiting 1, which is easy to
# miss inside a batch of other adds. That is exactly how the two 353-minute
# session logs were left out of 31c2df5 while appearing to have been added,
# and why docs/reports/.../index.html and the 19 Nov CSVs are in the repo only
# because somebody remembered `-f`.
#
# Re-included as a whole subtree rather than extension by extension, so the
# next report format is not a fourth instance of the same trap. This must stay
# BELOW the patterns it overrides and ABOVE __pycache__/, which still applies.
!docs/**

# Python bytecode from tools/.
__pycache__/
